\cf0 Samsung\'92s mobile unit (MX) operates with relatively thin margins compared to the semiconductor division. To increase the profitability of its hardware, Samsung has turned to three primary secondary revenue streams: pre-installation kickbacks, the Galaxy Store, and data monetization via its Customization Service.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 The Kickback Economy: Google and the "Search for Default"\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Samsung receives substantial payments from Google to ensure that Google Search and the Play Store remain the defaults on Galaxy devices. Between 2020 and 2023, Google paid Samsung $8 billion\'97approximately $2 billion per year\'97for this privilege. This "product placement" revenue is almost pure profit and serves to subsidize the manufacturing costs of the devices. If Samsung were to change its UI to be less addictive or to direct users away from Google\'92s services, it would risk losing this $2 billion annual subsidy.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 The Galaxy Store and the 20% Cut\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Samsung has aggressively revamped its own app store to capture more of the digital goods market. As of May 15, 2025, Samsung implemented a new revenue share model:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
80/20 Split
\f1\b0 : Developers receive 80% of net sales for paid apps and in-app items, while Samsung retains 20%.\
\ls1\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
85/15 Split
\f1\b0 : For subscription services, developers receive 85% and Samsung retains 15%.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 By undercutting the standard 30% commission of Apple and Google, Samsung hopes to entice high-engagement app developers to move users to the Galaxy Store versions of their apps. This creates a direct incentive for Samsung to ensure users are spending time and money within these apps.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 Customization Service and OS-Level Telemetry\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 Samsung\'92s "Customization Service" is the most direct mechanism for monetizing user behavior. When a user opts into this service (often during the initial setup process), Samsung collects:\
\pard\tx220\tx720\pardeftab720\li720\fi-720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \cf0 \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Browsing and Search History
\f1\b0 : Keywords and visited sites.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Communication Data
\f1\b0 : Incoming/outgoing call and text history to determine "who your most important contacts are".\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
Location Data
\f1\b0 : Precise geolocation through Bluetooth and Wi-Fi signals.\
\ls2\ilvl0
\f0\b \kerning1\expnd0\expndtw0 {\listtext	\uc0\u8226 	}\expnd0\expndtw0\kerning0
App Usage Statistics
\f1\b0 : Lists of installed apps and frequency of use.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0
\cf0 This data is used to "display customized advertisements about products and services" through Samsung Ads. By selling behavioral and demographic data to third-party partners, Samsung creates a recurring revenue stream from the user\'92s presence on the device. Every extra hour a user spends browsing or using apps provides more granular data points for Samsung to sell.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa298\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs36 \cf0 The Role of Social Media: TikTok and Meta\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 The user\'92s hypothesis regarding kickbacks from apps like TikTok is partially supported by industry practices. While "kickbacks" in the form of a percentage of ad revenue are rare, "pre-installation fees" are standard. Companies like TikTok and Meta pay manufacturers and carriers to ensure their apps are "bloatware"\'97pre-installed and sometimes un-deletable on certain models.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

\f0\b\fs28 \cf0 TikTok\'92s Financial Footprint\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f1\b0\fs24 \cf0 TikTok has become the "attention leader" in the mobile space, with users spending an average of 34 hours per month on the app. In 2024, TikTok generated $18 billion in advertising revenue in the US alone. ByteDance, its parent company, earned $120 billion in revenue in the same year.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

